The image of YPseqCode at depth 0 is the master neighbourhood of the first neighbourhood system, assuming the zero codes name the two masters.

The depth-zero atom-pair state is not junk and indexes both masters, and the X half-step atom at bit-source 0 has image the second master. The direct-refine index of that same state is the intersection of the first master with itself, hence the first master. The Y sub-step at bit 1 on this state is not junk, because otherwise the second master would meet itself emptily, and the split specification says that its positive piece is the first master. Antisymmetry uses the unconditional membership criterion: every point of the code lies in a non-junk atom of one of the two bits and hence in the master, and every master point lies in the bit-1 atom at index 0.
